<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia cuts price of Tapis crude for February.</title>
<headline>Malaysia cuts price of Tapis crude for February.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian state-owned Petronas has set its Tapis crude oil at $23.79 per barrel for February term liftings, down $2.44 from $26.23 in January, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Petronas also set a premium on March term liftings of 60 cents per barrel, down from 70 cents in February.  </p>
<p>The differentials for Labuan and Miri crude remained unchanged, at Tapis plus 15 cents for Labuan and Tapis plus 10 cents for Miri.</p>
<p>The Bintulu differential remained Tapis less 40 cents.</p>
<p>The price of February Dulang crude was set at $23.08, down from $25.66 in January.</p>
<p>PETRONAS 1996/1997 TERM PRICES (INCLUDES ALPHA ADJUSTMENT)</p>
<p>	   FEB     JAN	DEC	NOV    OCT     SEPT</p>
<p>TAPIS   $23.79  $26.23  $25.44   $25.06  $25.70  $23.01</p>
<p>LABUAN  $23.94  $26.38  $25.54   $25.16  $25.80  $23.11</p>
<p>MIRI    $23.89  $26.33  $25.34   $25.01  $25.60  $22.91</p>
<p>DULANG  $23.08  $25.66  $24.55   $24.10  $24.69  $22.11</p>
<p>BINTULU $23.39  $25.83  $25.14   $24.76  $25.40  $22.71</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703084)</p>
